WEBVTT

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:03.160
The starting point of MyTwin was

00:00:03.161 --> 00:00:04.800
MyTwin first, before MyTwinLab.

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:07.140
I'm going to explain to you

00:00:07.141 --> 00:00:08.280
what MyTwin is, above all.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:10.720
The starting point is

00:00:10.721 --> 00:00:12.180
simple: I lost both my parents,

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:14.720
my mother to a medical error,

00:00:14.721 --> 00:00:16.740
my father to a lack of

00:00:16.741 --> 00:00:18.320
prevention, on his own part.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.340
And when you're dealing with a medical

00:00:22.341 --> 00:00:24.120
emergency, when you're supporting

00:00:24.121 --> 00:00:25.680
your loved ones, or yourself,

00:00:25.681 --> 00:00:26.680
with regard to your own

00:00:26.681 --> 00:00:28.900
health, you're constantly

00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:29.780
searching for solutions.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:31.140
You're struggling.

00:00:32.119 --> 00:00:32.840
And you ask yourself: What's

00:00:32.841 --> 00:00:34.220
going on? I don't understand.

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:35.820
With doctors, you can feel that

00:00:35.821 --> 00:00:37.000
they don't necessarily have the time

00:00:37.001 --> 00:00:37.680
to answer us.

00:00:37.681 --> 00:00:39.040
We don't get the right answers.

00:00:39.041 --> 00:00:39.680
We sense that there may be

00:00:39.681 --> 00:00:40.420
solutions that exist

00:00:40.421 --> 00:00:41.340
somewhere, but we don't know where

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:42.080
they are, we don't know how

00:00:42.081 --> 00:00:42.800
they work, they're

00:00:42.801 --> 00:00:45.060
not... We saw that in a

00:00:45.061 --> 00:00:46.260
hospital, but in the end, they're

00:00:46.261 --> 00:00:47.100
no longer in place, it was

00:00:47.101 --> 00:00:48.020
just an experiment.

00:00:48.021 --> 00:00:50.520
So you end up asking yourself

00:00:50.521 --> 00:00:52.100
a lot of questions and searching

00:00:52.101 --> 00:00:53.360
for all this a bit desperately.

00:00:53.361 --> 00:00:54.440
So that's how I

00:00:54.441 --> 00:00:56.580
started telling myself: What are

00:00:56.581 --> 00:00:57.960
the solutions? Where are

00:00:57.961 --> 00:00:59.600
they? I'm going to find them, I'm

00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:00.860
going to identify them, and once

00:01:00.861 --> 00:01:02.120
and for all, I'm going to

00:01:02.121 --> 00:01:02.740
unify them.

00:01:02.741 --> 00:01:03.340
I'm going to bring them

00:01:03.341 --> 00:01:04.580
all together in one place.

00:01:04.581 --> 00:01:05.379
Because when you find a

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:07.220
solution for issues

00:01:07.221 --> 00:01:08.940
related to diabetes, maybe

00:01:08.941 --> 00:01:10.080
when you have diabetes, you

00:01:10.081 --> 00:01:11.080
also have endometriosis.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:12.320
Maybe you also have

00:01:12.321 --> 00:01:12.820
another disease.

00:01:12.821 --> 00:01:13.640
So actually, it makes no

00:01:13.641 --> 00:01:15.380
sense to have a single solution

00:01:15.381 --> 00:01:16.560
isolated in its own corner.

00:01:16.561 --> 00:01:17.600
All the solutions,

00:01:17.601 --> 00:01:19.240
the effective preventive ideas,

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:21.600
need to come together in one place,

00:01:21.601 --> 00:01:22.860
interact with one

00:01:22.861 --> 00:01:24.600
another and be able to talk to each other,

00:01:24.601 --> 00:01:27.940
communicate for the well-being

00:01:27.941 --> 00:01:28.320
of the patient.

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:29.360
So that's how

00:01:29.361 --> 00:01:30.520
MyTwin got started.

00:01:30.521 --> 00:01:31.760
And so, as you'll have understood,

00:01:31.761 --> 00:01:33.240
MyTwin is a solution that

00:01:33.241 --> 00:01:35.040
brings together within one

00:01:35.041 --> 00:01:36.860
single app all the

00:01:36.861 --> 00:01:37.880
solutions available on the

00:01:37.881 --> 00:01:38.860
market, the most

00:01:38.861 --> 00:01:40.280
advanced, the most reliable ones.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:43.860
With the goal of making everyone...

00:01:43.861 --> 00:01:44.960
of giving back to everyone

00:01:44.961 --> 00:01:46.360
control and knowledge

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:49.180
of their health, of information.

00:01:49.181 --> 00:01:50.940
In fact, there's a real desire

00:01:50.941 --> 00:01:52.900
for patients to no longer be

00:01:52.901 --> 00:01:55.140
in a kind of passivity

00:01:55.141 --> 00:01:56.260
regarding their health.

00:01:56.261 --> 00:01:57.280
That's what we call

00:01:57.281 --> 00:02:00.080
4P medicine: preventive, predictive,

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:03.040
personalized and proactive.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:07.100
We put back into the hands of the citizen,

00:02:07.101 --> 00:02:08.340
the end user, the

00:02:08.341 --> 00:02:10.880
patient, the right to information,

00:02:10.881 --> 00:02:12.280
access to information, access

00:02:12.281 --> 00:02:14.980
to care and the ability to

00:02:14.981 --> 00:02:16.700
trigger services with

00:02:16.701 --> 00:02:17.400
a single click.

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:19.600
And it's an app

00:02:19.601 --> 00:02:20.480
you have in your pocket

00:02:20.481 --> 00:02:21.940
on iOS or Android.

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:22.340
So it's very

00:02:22.341 --> 00:02:23.480
easy to use.

00:02:23.481 --> 00:02:24.400
So, a quick question,

00:02:24.401 --> 00:02:26.240
because doctors

00:02:26.241 --> 00:02:27.520
are very protective of their knowledge.

00:02:27.521 --> 00:02:29.200
How do they react when

00:02:29.201 --> 00:02:31.160
you offer this kind of

00:02:31.161 --> 00:02:32.600
solution? Is the medical

00:02:32.601 --> 00:02:34.260
profession skeptical? Or,

00:02:34.261 --> 00:02:37.260
on the contrary, are there doctors

00:02:37.261 --> 00:02:38.640
who understand that if the

00:02:38.641 --> 00:02:40.640
patient is informed and also

00:02:40.641 --> 00:02:42.120
in charge, once again

00:02:42.121 --> 00:02:44.400
responsible for their

00:02:44.401 --> 00:02:46.080
health, things go...

00:02:46.081 --> 00:02:47.440
it's complicated, I mean, to create

00:02:47.441 --> 00:02:48.980
a new solution like that

00:02:48.981 --> 00:02:51.140
in a very old-fashioned environment

00:02:51.141 --> 00:02:53.300
with codes of secrecy and

00:02:53.301 --> 00:02:55.100
not sharing information. Yeah,

00:02:55.101 --> 00:02:56.840
well, maybe I'm

00:02:56.841 --> 00:02:57.880
lucky, maybe I'm telling

00:02:57.881 --> 00:02:58.720
the right story.

00:02:58.721 --> 00:02:59.340
For now, we haven't had

00:02:59.341 --> 00:03:00.380
any particular problems, we've

00:03:00.381 --> 00:03:01.180
had enthusiasm, rather.

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:05.520
We've even... In fact, the

00:03:05.521 --> 00:03:06.580
common response I get every time from

00:03:06.581 --> 00:03:09.240
doctors or from executives in

00:03:09.241 --> 00:03:10.580
health institutions,

00:03:10.581 --> 00:03:14.120
insurers or others, is: Finally.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:17.000
Finally, a real opportunity.

00:03:17.001 --> 00:03:18.140
Finally, we know it's

00:03:18.141 --> 00:03:20.180
time to come together, to work

00:03:20.181 --> 00:03:22.200
together, it no longer makes sense otherwise.

00:03:22.201 --> 00:03:24.140
And above all, what makes

00:03:24.141 --> 00:03:26.000
everyone want to come together is that

00:03:26.001 --> 00:03:27.720
today, most health

00:03:27.721 --> 00:03:29.520
companies fail.

00:03:29.521 --> 00:03:31.340
80% of health companies in

00:03:31.341 --> 00:03:32.860
AI are going to,

00:03:32.861 --> 00:03:33.760
they're going to go under.

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:35.020
That's a reality.

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:36.120
So at some point,

00:03:36.121 --> 00:03:36.580
you have to do

00:03:36.581 --> 00:03:37.800
something, you have to react.

00:03:37.801 --> 00:03:39.180
So there, they see an

00:03:39.181 --> 00:03:41.000
opportunity and say: OK,

00:03:41.001 --> 00:03:42.000
this app is going to bring us together.

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:45.060
And then, there may be

00:03:45.061 --> 00:03:46.060
some resistant doctors, there

00:03:46.061 --> 00:03:48.640
certainly are, but it doesn't matter.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:50.380
For me, that's not my problem.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:53.200
Yes, you take those who are

00:03:53.201 --> 00:03:54.880
willing and who

00:03:54.881 --> 00:03:55.680
understand your project.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:58.520
So MyTwinLab is

00:03:58.521 --> 00:03:59.280
another project.

00:03:59.281 --> 00:04:02.000
I mean, it's MyTwin on a broader scale, with

00:04:02.001 --> 00:04:04.080
other partners? Yes, so what

00:04:04.081 --> 00:04:05.320
you need to understand about MyTwin,

00:04:05.321 --> 00:04:07.620
first, is that, here, I've

00:04:07.621 --> 00:04:08.760
explained it simply: it's

00:04:08.761 --> 00:04:10.180
an app that

00:04:10.181 --> 00:04:11.520
integrates lots of apps in one

00:04:11.521 --> 00:04:13.220
place so that we have

00:04:13.221 --> 00:04:14.580
complete access to all the health

00:04:14.581 --> 00:04:15.440
solutions.

00:04:15.441 --> 00:04:16.420
Which is already very, very good.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:18.459
But beyond that,

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:19.700
the mission and vision we have

00:04:19.701 --> 00:04:20.920
are bigger than all of us, because we

00:04:20.921 --> 00:04:21.760
are creating what we

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:22.740
call a digital twin.

00:04:22.741 --> 00:04:23.400
Now, you're in

00:04:23.401 --> 00:04:24.100
tech, so

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:25.340
you know what that is.

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:26.560
Why? Because

00:04:26.561 --> 00:04:27.720
quite simply, as soon as

00:04:27.721 --> 00:04:29.580
your medical record is

00:04:29.581 --> 00:04:31.860
connected to an LLM and, on top of

00:04:31.861 --> 00:04:33.680
that, it's going to be connected to all

00:04:33.681 --> 00:04:35.340
the health apps within

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:36.680
one single place, you

00:04:36.681 --> 00:04:37.400
start to have quite a lot

00:04:37.401 --> 00:04:38.700
of information about a person.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:40.660
And eventually, it can start

00:04:40.661 --> 00:04:41.720
to create, let's say,

00:04:41.721 --> 00:04:43.640
the avatar, the digital twin

00:04:43.641 --> 00:04:44.380
of that person.

00:04:44.381 --> 00:04:45.580
And that's what we do.

00:04:45.581 --> 00:04:46.820
We're creating the most advanced

00:04:46.821 --> 00:04:47.960
digital twin of patient

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:49.860
health in the world.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:51.620
Why? Because it's

00:04:51.621 --> 00:04:52.740
thanks to a community.

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:54.060
And that may be the

00:04:54.061 --> 00:04:57.040
difference with ChatGPT Health...

00:04:57.041 --> 00:04:57.980
or Claude for Healthcare.

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.120
What we tell ourselves is, given

00:05:00.121 --> 00:05:00.980
that I started from

00:05:00.981 --> 00:05:03.220
my point of view as a citizen patient

00:05:03.221 --> 00:05:05.400
who had, who has, well, who had

00:05:05.401 --> 00:05:06.480
setbacks in healthcare with

00:05:06.481 --> 00:05:08.900
my parents, the first

00:05:08.901 --> 00:05:10.120
thing we tell ourselves is

00:05:10.121 --> 00:05:10.820
ultimately, as

00:05:10.821 --> 00:05:11.900
a user, as a

00:05:11.901 --> 00:05:14.060
patient, when we use AI,

00:05:14.061 --> 00:05:15.940
whatever it may be, or when

00:05:15.941 --> 00:05:16.920
we use tools like

00:05:16.921 --> 00:05:19.200
this one, why shouldn't I

00:05:19.201 --> 00:05:21.320
also be involved in

00:05:21.321 --> 00:05:23.320
building these tools? Knowing

00:05:23.321 --> 00:05:24.960
how we're building ourselves.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:26.660
What are our ideas for

00:05:26.661 --> 00:05:28.460
tomorrow? What are the

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:29.380
next features

00:05:29.381 --> 00:05:30.720
we're going to roll out? Do

00:05:30.721 --> 00:05:31.600
you have

00:05:31.601 --> 00:05:32.900
skills to help us

00:05:32.901 --> 00:05:33.620
create these next

00:05:33.621 --> 00:05:35.080
features? That's

00:05:35.081 --> 00:05:35.760
MyTwinLab.

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:38.380
Being able to welcome into the

00:05:38.381 --> 00:05:39.820
lab the average

00:05:39.821 --> 00:05:41.380
person, who can quite

00:05:41.381 --> 00:05:42.460
simply tell us their

00:05:42.461 --> 00:05:43.380
health story, which is

00:05:43.381 --> 00:05:45.360
already data that's very

00:05:45.361 --> 00:05:46.860
valuable, because feedback,

00:05:46.861 --> 00:05:48.140
stories,

00:05:48.141 --> 00:05:49.860
anecdotes are what drive and

00:05:49.861 --> 00:05:50.900
what trigger emotion

00:05:50.901 --> 00:05:51.800
and collective movement.

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:53.720
First level of contribution,

00:05:53.721 --> 00:05:54.860
very simple: share your

00:05:54.861 --> 00:05:55.820
health story, we all have

00:05:55.821 --> 00:05:56.720
one, we all have them.

00:05:57.520 --> 00:05:58.780
Second level of contribution:

00:05:58.781 --> 00:06:00.000
I'm a tech person, I'm a

00:06:00.001 --> 00:06:01.180
doctor, I'm a researcher,

00:06:01.181 --> 00:06:01.900
I'm a student, I'm

00:06:01.901 --> 00:06:02.960
passionate about health,

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:04.400
I want to go further.

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:06.500
And then, we can actually

00:06:06.501 --> 00:06:08.160
create the next features

00:06:08.161 --> 00:06:09.320
together, AIs that

00:06:09.321 --> 00:06:09.920
will be able

00:06:10.468 --> 00:06:12.028
to read an X-ray better.

00:06:12.029 --> 00:06:13.408
We're working on endometriosis

00:06:13.409 --> 00:06:15.088
at the moment, on the brain,

00:06:15.848 --> 00:06:16.728
other features that

00:06:16.729 --> 00:06:17.788
matter to you in terms of

00:06:17.789 --> 00:06:19.148
your values, in terms of your

00:06:19.149 --> 00:06:20.888
issues, which are

00:06:20.889 --> 00:06:22.488
your own, and in terms of your

00:06:22.489 --> 00:06:23.128
sensitivities.

00:06:23.129 --> 00:06:24.808
Tools should reflect who you are,

00:06:24.809 --> 00:06:26.408
what you

00:06:26.409 --> 00:06:27.348
are and what you

00:06:27.349 --> 00:06:28.928
want to become. So we're all

00:06:29.588 --> 00:06:30.728
about community, building

00:06:30.729 --> 00:06:32.308
community and the contribution

00:06:32.309 --> 00:06:32.568
of members.

00:06:33.368 --> 00:06:34.468
So, we clearly understand the

00:06:34.469 --> 00:06:36.368
difference compared to ChatGPT

00:06:36.369 --> 00:06:37.648
Health, especially since

00:06:37.649 --> 00:06:38.908
obviously, all the LLMs are

00:06:38.909 --> 00:06:40.588
creating their own services.

00:06:41.168 --> 00:06:42.328
It's no coincidence that they've

00:06:42.329 --> 00:06:44.808
moved into this data and

00:06:44.809 --> 00:06:46.008
into this form of support.

00:06:47.108 --> 00:06:48.188
For you, when we talk about

00:06:48.189 --> 00:06:50.188
ChatGPT Health, what

00:06:50.788 --> 00:06:52.628
opportunity or danger do you see? Well,

00:06:52.629 --> 00:06:54.008
when you heard that announcement,

00:06:54.009 --> 00:06:55.188
how did you react? I mean, how did it

00:06:55.189 --> 00:06:56.728
make you feel, as an entrepreneur,

00:06:56.729 --> 00:06:58.728
but also as a citizen,

00:06:58.729 --> 00:07:00.828
a patient, knowing where

00:07:00.829 --> 00:07:01.308
your data is?

00:07:01.928 --> 00:07:03.628
So, what was your reaction

00:07:03.629 --> 00:07:05.248
to an announcement that was

00:07:05.249 --> 00:07:06.708
pretty big three weeks ago,

00:07:06.709 --> 00:07:08.188
I think? Yes, three

00:07:08.189 --> 00:07:10.988
weeks ago, ChatGPT Health came out, and two

00:07:10.989 --> 00:07:13.348
days later, Claude for Healthcare, and

00:07:13.349 --> 00:07:14.828
I hope that in a while,

00:07:14.829 --> 00:07:16.988
Mistral Health, that would be the

00:07:16.989 --> 00:07:17.268
logical next step.

00:07:17.948 --> 00:07:19.348
So, personally,

00:07:19.349 --> 00:07:20.488
I had two reactions.

00:07:20.489 --> 00:07:22.668
The first, very positive.

00:07:22.669 --> 00:07:23.828
I'm convinced that the

00:07:23.829 --> 00:07:25.008
world of tomorrow will be incredible.

00:07:25.009 --> 00:07:26.128
I'm a very positive person by nature.

00:07:27.568 --> 00:07:28.208
And I think that's

00:07:28.209 --> 00:07:29.328
important in the story we

00:07:29.329 --> 00:07:30.128
tell and in the choices we

00:07:30.129 --> 00:07:30.948
make, in the media.

00:07:30.949 --> 00:07:31.788
If we're positive,

00:07:31.789 --> 00:07:32.848
we'll create positive things.

00:07:33.488 --> 00:07:34.188
We'll think about it that way.

00:07:34.748 --> 00:07:36.628
Anyway, first positive reaction:

00:07:36.629 --> 00:07:39.628
first of all, for us,

00:07:39.629 --> 00:07:41.228
it allowed us to position ourselves

00:07:41.229 --> 00:07:43.188
and to say: That's it.

00:07:43.189 --> 00:07:44.008
Some pretty big players

00:07:44.009 --> 00:07:46.368
are getting into this. The evolution,

00:07:46.369 --> 00:07:47.768
it was expected.

00:07:47.769 --> 00:07:48.908
We knew it was going to happen.

00:07:48.909 --> 00:07:49.908
We'd been doing it ourselves in our

00:07:49.909 --> 00:07:51.888
own corner for over a year already.

00:07:52.548 --> 00:07:53.768
So positive, because for us, as

00:07:53.769 --> 00:07:55.148
a player, it gives us

00:07:55.149 --> 00:07:56.348
something to aim for,

00:07:56.349 --> 00:07:57.588
to position ourselves, to look at

00:07:57.589 --> 00:07:58.568
what they're going to do.

00:07:58.569 --> 00:07:59.888
And ultimately, for us, what

00:07:59.889 --> 00:08:01.368
market share we're going to take.

00:08:01.369 --> 00:08:02.188
We're a company,

00:08:02.189 --> 00:08:02.868
we have to make money.

00:08:03.448 --> 00:08:04.748
So how are we going to position ourselves?

00:08:04.749 --> 00:08:05.288
What's our

00:08:05.289 --> 00:08:06.348
storytelling going to be? What's our

00:08:06.349 --> 00:08:08.448
message going to be? And, ultimately, what

00:08:08.449 --> 00:08:09.628
market are we going to

00:08:09.629 --> 00:08:10.748
conquer? And how are we going to

00:08:10.749 --> 00:08:12.428
position ourselves with that? First

00:08:12.429 --> 00:08:13.508
very positive thing for us.

00:08:14.048 --> 00:08:15.348
Second positive thing too, because

00:08:15.349 --> 00:08:17.068
it's a disruptive innovation

00:08:17.069 --> 00:08:19.027
that moves all of healthcare forward,

00:08:19.028 --> 00:08:19.888
which means that, behind it,

00:08:19.889 --> 00:08:21.728
it inevitably makes us ask questions.

00:08:21.729 --> 00:08:22.788
Here we are today,

00:08:22.789 --> 00:08:23.468
doctors are starting to

00:08:23.469 --> 00:08:24.408
talk about it, health

00:08:24.409 --> 00:08:25.108
institutions are talking about it, they're

00:08:25.109 --> 00:08:26.528
saying: Wait, we're out of

00:08:26.529 --> 00:08:28.428
time, we need to act. That's

00:08:28.429 --> 00:08:29.148
very positive.

00:08:29.848 --> 00:08:32.548
The other side is: Ah, yet another

00:08:32.549 --> 00:08:34.028
company, if I'm caricaturing,

00:08:34.727 --> 00:08:35.748
that's going to dominate the world,

00:08:36.268 --> 00:08:38.707
and this time, in the health sector.

00:08:38.708 --> 00:08:40.628
What do we do? Well, we've

00:08:40.629 --> 00:08:42.268
made the choice of saying that

00:08:42.269 --> 00:08:43.587
our product, we're creating it with you

00:08:44.227 --> 00:08:45.108
and we're creating it together.

00:08:45.109 --> 00:08:45.908
And why not even,

00:08:45.909 --> 00:08:46.528
at some point,

00:08:46.529 --> 00:08:47.508
own it together.

00:08:47.509 --> 00:08:48.608
We could very well share the

00:08:48.609 --> 00:08:49.868
shares of our business

00:08:50.408 --> 00:08:51.748
with the community of users.

00:08:51.749 --> 00:08:53.408
For us, it's super important

00:08:53.409 --> 00:08:54.688
to head in that direction, eventually.

00:08:56.068 --> 00:08:56.988
So, I think that's the

00:08:56.989 --> 00:08:58.008
danger point: telling

00:08:58.009 --> 00:09:00.928
ourselves we're going to end up again

00:09:00.929 --> 00:09:03.008
in 10 years with one, two,

00:09:03.009 --> 00:09:04.208
three companies that are going to

00:09:04.209 --> 00:09:05.928
dominate the market and that

00:09:05.929 --> 00:09:07.348
will eventually be able to do whatever

00:09:07.349 --> 00:09:07.948
they want.

00:09:09.828 --> 00:09:10.948
But it's not just because

00:09:10.949 --> 00:09:12.688
they're American.

00:09:12.689 --> 00:09:13.928
And that's maybe a

00:09:13.929 --> 00:09:15.008
slightly different point,

00:09:15.808 --> 00:09:17.268
but we can have

00:09:17.269 --> 00:09:18.548
European or French players.

00:09:19.328 --> 00:09:20.388
Being French doesn't mean

00:09:20.389 --> 00:09:22.168
you necessarily do the right

00:09:22.169 --> 00:09:22.928
things in the long run.

00:09:24.948 --> 00:09:26.248
All the health players that

00:09:26.249 --> 00:09:27.168
are succeeding today

00:09:27.169 --> 00:09:28.408
in AI for prediction and

00:09:28.409 --> 00:09:30.888
prevention, their market

00:09:30.889 --> 00:09:33.648
is 80% in the US or in Asia.

00:09:35.148 --> 00:09:36.508
When they get bought out,

00:09:36.509 --> 00:09:37.088
when the investment funds

00:09:37.089 --> 00:09:38.768
exit, etc., what choices

00:09:38.769 --> 00:09:40.008
will they make? We have no idea.

00:09:40.548 --> 00:09:42.428
For us, the only safeguard

00:09:42.429 --> 00:09:44.108
we've found is to say

00:09:44.109 --> 00:09:45.308
from day one, we're

00:09:45.309 --> 00:09:47.028
building with the users.

00:09:47.029 --> 00:09:47.928
It's the users who

00:09:47.929 --> 00:09:49.308
co-create the solutions and

00:09:49.309 --> 00:09:50.328
who co-own the solutions.

00:09:50.908 --> 00:09:51.828
So an entrepreneur's

00:09:51.829 --> 00:09:54.288
responsibility with a vision of

00:09:54.289 --> 00:09:56.248
the common good, of sharing from the

00:09:56.249 --> 00:09:58.688
start, indeed, outside of a

00:09:58.689 --> 00:10:01.168
purely capitalist logic, but

00:10:01.169 --> 00:10:02.388
aware that there are indeed

00:10:02.389 --> 00:10:03.608
monopolies that need to be

00:10:03.609 --> 00:10:05.268
fought, that are

00:10:05.269 --> 00:10:07.088
forming. After that, everyone is free

00:10:07.089 --> 00:10:09.348
to choose the solution based

00:10:09.349 --> 00:10:11.548
on their values or on where they're

00:10:11.549 --> 00:10:13.568
willing to hand over their

00:10:13.569 --> 00:10:15.168
personal data, their health data.

00:10:15.728 --> 00:10:17.148
To wrap up, since you're

00:10:17.149 --> 00:10:18.328
positive, you're optimistic, it's

00:10:18.329 --> 00:10:20.248
rather nice to

00:10:20.249 --> 00:10:21.368
hear, because I'm

00:10:21.369 --> 00:10:22.408
kind of... I share your

00:10:22.409 --> 00:10:23.848
feeling that negative self-fulfilling

00:10:23.849 --> 00:10:26.068
prophecies, there are

00:10:26.069 --> 00:10:26.568
a lot of them.

00:10:27.748 --> 00:10:30.448
What's the future of healthcare? In

00:10:30.449 --> 00:10:32.988
2050, what's your picture of

00:10:32.989 --> 00:10:35.388
what healthcare will be like? I think that

00:10:35.389 --> 00:10:38.768
within 10 years, Léa, 70% of the

00:10:38.769 --> 00:10:40.008
world's population will have

00:10:40.009 --> 00:10:41.028
their health digital twin

00:10:41.029 --> 00:10:41.388
in their pocket.

00:10:42.128 --> 00:10:43.268
In my opinion, it's a certainty.

00:10:43.269 --> 00:10:44.488
There's already ChatGPT Health, so it's

00:10:44.489 --> 00:10:45.668
a first, a first

00:10:45.669 --> 00:10:46.748
building block, a first start.

00:10:47.488 --> 00:10:48.188
A lot of people

00:10:48.189 --> 00:10:49.168
use GPT, so

00:10:49.169 --> 00:10:50.248
it's going to move very, very fast.

00:10:50.249 --> 00:10:51.048
And you know, I was saying this a

00:10:51.049 --> 00:10:52.068
year ago and at one point, people said:

00:10:52.069 --> 00:10:52.728
You might be a little

00:10:52.729 --> 00:10:54.108
optimistic. Now...

00:10:54.109 --> 00:10:54.848
it's reality.

00:10:55.768 --> 00:10:57.468
So, I think we'll all have

00:10:57.469 --> 00:10:58.948
our digital twin, our

00:10:58.949 --> 00:11:00.348
virtual representation

00:11:00.349 --> 00:11:01.148
of our health and our

00:11:01.149 --> 00:11:02.828
body in our pocket,

00:11:02.829 --> 00:11:03.948
like the one we're creating.

00:11:04.748 --> 00:11:06.588
And we'll be able to access

00:11:06.589 --> 00:11:07.648
almost all possible health

00:11:07.649 --> 00:11:09.228
services in terms

00:11:09.229 --> 00:11:10.828
of prediction and prevention.

00:11:10.829 --> 00:11:12.448
So, we'll be very proactive.

00:11:12.449 --> 00:11:13.768
And at the same time, the LLM

00:11:13.769 --> 00:11:52.448
will be there to guide us through

00:11:52.449 --> 00:11:56.268
our care pathway in

00:11:56.269 --> 00:11:57.148
a very personalized way.

00:11:58.388 --> 00:12:02.348
For us, there will be as many MyTwin

00:12:02.349 --> 00:12:03.288
apps as there are users.

00:12:03.289 --> 00:12:06.088
If you're a woman and you have

00:12:06.089 --> 00:12:07.448
endometriosis, you... Thank you

00:12:07.449 --> 00:12:09.188
very much, Rubens, for these

00:12:09.189 --> 00:12:11.208
positive words, which also feel good.

00:12:12.148 --> 00:12:13.008
Do you have any

00:12:13.009 --> 00:12:14.248
questions? We have time to

00:12:14.249 --> 00:12:15.348
take one or two questions,

00:12:15.349 --> 00:12:17.428
if health inspires you

00:12:17.429 --> 00:12:18.408
or if you have any questions

00:12:18.409 --> 00:12:20.068
about the work of

00:12:20.069 --> 00:12:21.888
Rubens, of Ystart.

00:12:23.692 --> 00:12:24.852
No? We've worn you out.

00:12:26.232 --> 00:12:28.252
Well, thank you very much, Rubens.

00:12:28.253 --> 00:12:29.412
I'm just going to... There was a

00:12:29.413 --> 00:12:31.492
question? Sorry, I didn't see.

00:12:32.052 --> 00:12:32.752
I'm not from the younger

00:12:32.753 --> 00:12:34.272
generation, I'm from the older one.

00:12:35.332 --> 00:12:35.732
Hello.

00:12:36.472 --> 00:12:37.352
So I'm from the older

00:12:37.353 --> 00:12:40.552
generation, and I have a bit of trouble

00:12:40.553 --> 00:12:43.392
understanding how all this,

00:12:43.912 --> 00:12:45.912
this dematerialized material,

00:12:45.913 --> 00:12:47.292
can materialize.

00:12:48.032 --> 00:12:49.252
In the example you're giving

00:12:49.253 --> 00:12:51.012
about healthcare, I hear

00:12:51.013 --> 00:12:51.732
that you're talking about a

00:12:51.733 --> 00:12:53.372
digital twin, but on the

00:12:53.373 --> 00:12:55.072
other hand, in France at least,

00:12:55.073 --> 00:12:57.352
we don't have doctors, we have

00:12:57.353 --> 00:12:58.832
appointment waiting times that are

00:12:59.512 --> 00:13:00.672
immeasurable.

00:13:00.673 --> 00:13:02.812
And so, I have trouble

00:13:02.813 --> 00:13:06.192
understanding how we can move forward

00:13:06.193 --> 00:13:08.172
in a dematerialized field

00:13:08.173 --> 00:13:10.292
when, in practice, we won't be able...

00:13:10.293 --> 00:13:11.352
I mean, it's nice to have a

00:13:11.353 --> 00:13:12.312
digital twin, but if you can't

00:13:12.313 --> 00:13:13.572
get treated, what's

00:13:13.573 --> 00:13:16.412
the point? So, your question, there

00:13:16.413 --> 00:13:17.652
are indeed two issues,

00:13:17.653 --> 00:13:18.832
which run in parallel and

00:13:18.833 --> 00:13:19.512
move forward together.

00:13:19.513 --> 00:13:20.292
And that's why we also work

00:13:20.293 --> 00:13:21.432
with institutions

00:13:22.132 --> 00:13:23.672
and the top medical directors

00:13:23.673 --> 00:13:24.752
of health insurers and others

00:13:24.753 --> 00:13:26.812
to see how the demands

00:13:26.813 --> 00:13:28.492
will manage to move forward.

00:13:28.493 --> 00:13:30.152
First part of the answer:

00:13:30.812 --> 00:13:31.772
it's demographic.

00:13:31.773 --> 00:13:33.632
Unfortunately, we have a

00:13:33.633 --> 00:13:34.672
population that is increasingly

00:13:34.673 --> 00:13:35.712
aging, and a number

00:13:35.713 --> 00:13:36.952
of healthcare workers that's shrinking.

00:13:36.953 --> 00:13:39.092
So factually, we're going to be

00:13:39.093 --> 00:13:40.252
more and more in a care crisis.

00:13:40.912 --> 00:13:41.492
That's for sure.

00:13:42.152 --> 00:13:42.712
We absolutely don't want

00:13:42.713 --> 00:13:43.932
to separate the two.

00:13:43.933 --> 00:13:45.272
That is to say, the digital

00:13:45.273 --> 00:13:46.972
twin, for us, must be

00:13:46.973 --> 00:13:48.792
used by the patient and also

00:13:48.793 --> 00:13:50.552
by the doctor to be able to

00:13:50.553 --> 00:13:52.372
improve patient follow-up.

00:13:52.373 --> 00:13:52.932
So that means

00:13:52.933 --> 00:13:54.392
that indeed, I agree,

00:13:54.393 --> 00:13:55.352
our idea is to say

00:13:56.072 --> 00:13:57.772
yes, we have one more tool in

00:13:57.773 --> 00:13:59.332
our pocket, but that means

00:13:59.333 --> 00:14:00.192
you still always need

00:14:00.193 --> 00:14:01.492
to be with your doctor.

00:14:01.493 --> 00:14:02.572
So that means we still need

00:14:02.573 --> 00:14:04.272
just as many healthcare workers.

00:14:04.273 --> 00:14:05.152
What's the answer to

00:14:05.153 --> 00:14:06.332
having more healthcare workers tomorrow

00:14:06.872 --> 00:14:08.352
and being even better supported?

00:14:08.892 --> 00:14:10.032
I don't have the answer.

00:14:10.033 --> 00:14:10.872
If I did, I think

00:14:11.692 --> 00:14:13.052
it would be fantastic.

00:14:13.053 --> 00:14:14.172
Nobody has it today.

00:14:14.712 --> 00:14:15.772
And unfortunately, there's this

00:14:15.773 --> 00:14:16.632
demographic aspect

00:14:16.633 --> 00:14:17.852
that means we have it

00:14:17.853 --> 00:14:18.712
less and less, the answer.

00:14:20.292 --> 00:14:21.472
Now, what's going to be

00:14:21.473 --> 00:14:23.492
interesting is that the...

00:14:24.032 --> 00:14:25.812
there are going to be

00:14:25.813 --> 00:14:28.252
new, I think, new

00:14:29.792 --> 00:14:31.212
coordinators among

00:14:31.213 --> 00:14:32.232
healthcare workers emerging.

00:14:33.112 --> 00:14:34.032
The big issue,

00:14:34.572 --> 00:14:35.912
what you're explaining, ultimately,

00:14:35.913 --> 00:14:37.212
ties in with the notion

00:14:37.213 --> 00:14:38.692
of care coordination.

00:14:38.693 --> 00:14:39.852
Who's going to coordinate care?

00:14:39.853 --> 00:14:41.152
Who's going to support us,

00:14:41.153 --> 00:14:42.832
humanly speaking, along our

00:14:42.833 --> 00:14:45.072
care pathway? We don't have enough

00:14:45.073 --> 00:14:46.312
radiologists, we don't

00:14:46.313 --> 00:14:47.752
have enough dermatologists.

00:14:48.312 --> 00:14:49.432
So ultimately, who's going to do it?

00:14:50.132 --> 00:14:51.692
There are healthcare workers, so

00:14:51.693 --> 00:14:53.172
nurses, who today have

00:14:53.173 --> 00:14:55.572
an already well-established role, but

00:14:55.573 --> 00:14:56.732
who can also have this

00:14:56.733 --> 00:14:59.092
ability to take on this work of

00:14:59.093 --> 00:15:00.432
coordination and to be able to

00:15:00.433 --> 00:15:01.772
meet certain needs to

00:15:01.773 --> 00:15:02.612
a certain extent.

00:15:02.613 --> 00:15:04.092
It doesn't solve every problem,

00:15:04.093 --> 00:15:05.132
but there are going to be what we call,

00:15:05.133 --> 00:15:07.092
roughly, care coordinators

00:15:07.093 --> 00:15:08.052
entering the market.

00:15:08.053 --> 00:15:09.592
They could be nurses,

00:15:09.593 --> 00:15:11.032
male or female, they could be

00:15:11.033 --> 00:15:11.892
other types of healthcare workers, they

00:15:11.893 --> 00:15:13.432
could be, why not, APA,

00:15:13.433 --> 00:15:14.632
APA coaches, in adapted

00:15:14.633 --> 00:15:15.752
physical activity, why not

00:15:15.753 --> 00:15:17.732
physiotherapists, who will take on

00:15:17.733 --> 00:15:19.212
other roles to come

00:15:19.992 --> 00:15:21.512
improve and strengthen

00:15:21.513 --> 00:15:22.832
care coordination at the

00:15:22.833 --> 00:15:23.312
national level.

00:15:23.852 --> 00:15:25.152
So, there are answers,

00:15:25.153 --> 00:15:26.272
partial answers,

00:15:26.273 --> 00:15:26.992
but on the other hand, the demographic

00:15:26.993 --> 00:15:28.932
problem, that one we don't have.
